schema: "0.4"
id: phosphor-14-kb-maintenance-console
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns (a CLI learning tool) — KB Maintenance Console, a dense TUI ops surface. HERO screen.
# Theme tenets: monochrome amber CRT, single glowing hue on warm near-black, fixed-width mono as the primary UI face, radius 0, box-drawing chrome, zero elevation.
# Palette: amber #ffb000, warm near-black #140c00, dim amber #c88a00, bright amber #ffd050; warning stays amber and is prefixed "! " (no error red on this screen).

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    monochrome amber-CRT terminal — ONE warm amber hue on a warm near-black void,
    fixed-width monospace as the primary UI face for everything, radius 0, box-drawing
    chrome, zero elevation. Terse, machine, all-business register — the UI reports, it
    does not decorate. This is a dense TUI ops console in a real terminal, never a web
    page.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a single amber-on-black TERMINAL WINDOW showing a
    dense KB MAINTENANCE CONSOLE — a text-mode "mission control" for a command-line
    knowledge base, built entirely from box-drawing panes. Fill the frame with ONE
    terminal window and a thin top title bar; there is NO web browser chrome, no tabs,
    no address bar, no rounded website panels.

    One warm AMBER hue on a warm near-black background; hierarchy comes from BRIGHTNESS
    (dim vs bright amber), never other colors. Fixed-width monospaced type everywhere.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (box-drawing panes, top to bottom):

    TOP RULE: a horizontal box-drawing rule with a notched title "┤ KB MAINTENANCE ├" at
    the left and a right-aligned path "kb: ~/.config/the-robot-learns-kb".

    STAT TILE ROW: a row of four box-drawn STAT TILES, each a small rectangular
    box-drawing region with no fill (the void shows through): a big bright-amber number
    over a dim-amber label — "1,284 ARTICLES", "37 DECKS", "12 ORPHANS", "INDEX ok". The
    numbers are the brightest thing on screen.

    WARNING BANNER: a full-width box-drawn banner, still amber (warning is amber, not
    red), prefixed with a bold "! " glyph — "! schema drift: 3 files fail their governing
    schema". Amber text, glyph-led so meaning never rests on color alone.

    VALIDATION OUTPUT PANE: a box-drawn pane titled "┤ VALIDATE ├" with a scroll of
    monospaced result rows, each led by a glyph and differentiated by amber intensity:
    "✓ 1,281 files ok", "✗ 3 files fail schema", "i 4 duplicate candidates found",
    "· reindex not required". Keep it grid-aligned like real tool output.

    CONFIRMATION PROMPT: a flat box-drawn confirmation region (no shadow) laid over a
    slightly dimmed backdrop, titled "┤ CONFIRM ├", reading "prune 12 stale articles?"
    with two bracketed mono buttons "[ y ]" and "[ N ]" where the default "[ N ]" is
    drawn as reverse-video (amber fill, near-black text).

    BOTTOM STATUS RULE: a persistent reverse-video status bar across the full width with
    keybind hints "^V validate   ^R reindex   ^P prune   ^Q quit".

    PALETTE & TYPE: monochrome warm amber on warm near-black — one glowing amber with dim
    and bright steps, nothing else; no green, blue, or rainbow. Status is shown by glyphs
    (✓ ✗ ! i ·) and brightness, not by hue. Fixed-width terminal font throughout, no
    proportional or sans typeface anywhere.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: zero rounded corners — every pane is a sharp rectangle bounded by
    thin amber box-drawing rules at reduced intensity, an active pane's rule brighter; no
    drop shadows, gradients, glow bloom, scanlines, or screen curvature. Flat amber light
    on a dark void.

    MOOD: a dense, capable retro ops console — one amber, box-drawing everywhere, all
    business, a machine keeping its own house in order.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, web browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, rounded website cards, syntax-highlighting rainbow, green terminal text, CRT scanlines, screen glow bloom, screen curvature"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Reads as a dense KB maintenance TUI: titled top rule with kb path, a row of box-drawn stat tiles (article/deck/orphan/index), an amber glyph-led warning banner, a validation output pane with ✓/✗/i/· rows, a flat confirmation prompt with bracketed buttons, and a bottom keybind status rule"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Monochrome amber on warm near-black, fixed-width mono for ALL text, radius 0, box-drawing panes not shadowed cards, status by glyph+brightness not hue"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Instrument-dense but grid-aligned; clear hierarchy with the stat numbers brightest; plausible real TUI console"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts, no CRT filter kitsch"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "web browser chrome or a marketing web page instead of a terminal window"
    - "more than one hue (green/blue/rainbow) instead of monochrome amber"

tags: [phosphor, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup]
